---
source: crates/agentgateway/src/import.rs
description: src/tests/import/litellm/cache-settings.yaml
---
source: litellm
config:
  config:
    database:
      url: "sqlite://data.db"
  gateways:
    default:
      port: 4000
  ui:
    gateways: default
  llm:
    gateways: default
    models:
      - name: chat
        provider: openAI
        params:
          model: gpt-4o
findings:
  - sourcePath: "model_list[0]"
    status: exact
    message: Imported model deployment for chat
  - sourcePath: router_settings.redis_url
    status: manual
    message: "LiteLLM router Redis coordination settings were not emitted; review shared routing, cooldown, and usage state separately from response caching. These settings can also configure the backend when router response caching is enabled"
  - sourcePath: router_settings.cache_responses
    status: manual
    message: This LiteLLM response-cache flag is false and was not emitted; review other response-cache settings independently
  - sourcePath: router_settings.caching_groups
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache sharing across model groups was not preserved; review cache-key isolation when configuring response caching manually
  - sourcePath: "router_settings.caching_groups[0]"
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache sharing across model groups was not preserved; review cache-key isolation when configuring response caching manually
  - sourcePath: "router_settings.caching_groups[0][0]"
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache sharing across model groups was not preserved; review cache-key isolation when configuring response caching manually
  - sourcePath: "router_settings.caching_groups[0][1]"
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache sharing across model groups was not preserved; review cache-key isolation when configuring response caching manually
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response caching was requested but was not preserved; configure a response-cache solution manually before relying on cached responses. Provider promptCaching is not equivalent to caching complete responses
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.type
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache backend selection was not emitted; choose a response-cache solution manually. Provider promptCaching does not cache complete responses
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.host
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache connection or authentication settings were not emitted; configure connectivity and secret references in the chosen cache solution manually
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.password
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache connection or authentication settings were not emitted; configure connectivity and secret references in the chosen cache solution manually
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.ttl
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache expiration was not preserved; review TTL units and backend defaults when configuring cache lifetime manually
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.namespace
    status: manual
    message: LiteLLM response-cache namespace was not preserved; configure cache-key isolation manually before sharing a cache backend
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.future_setting
    status: unsupported
    message: Unrecognized LiteLLM response-cache parameter was not emitted; review it in the chosen cache solution
  - sourcePath: litellm_settings.cache_params.future_setting.nested
    status: unsupported
    message: Unrecognized LiteLLM response-cache parameter was not emitted; review it in the chosen cache solution
